	<!-- the dialogs -->
	<string id="shelter_sid_laptop_0">
		<text>A group of stalkers ordered a laptop from you. The ones who settled in the bunker.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sid_laptop_1">
		<text>That they did. Ordered it, paid up, and nobody came to collect. I thought somebody did them in.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sid_laptop_2">
		<text>Worse. They're zombified, wandering around their bunker.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sid_laptop_3">
		<text>Damn... Shame about the lads, good customers: paid up front, never haggled. Fine, the laptop's yours, but not for a thank-you. Sakharov owes me a container of artefacts, and my legs aren't government issue. Go to Yantar, bring it here, and you get the laptop.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sid_laptop_4">
		<text>Deal.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sid_container_0">
		<text>Brought your container from Sakharov.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sid_container_1">
		<text>I see, I see. Back aching? That's no bottle of vodka. Here's your laptop. And mind: I'm not in the business of charging it. Find your own power, a generator or an anomaly.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sid_container_2">
		<text>Thanks for that much.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sakharov_0">
		<text>Professor, Sidorovich sent me. He says you have a container for him.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sakharov_1">
		<text>Ah, the container... Yes, yes, samples for our mutual acquaintance. A warning, young man: the case is a heavy one and its cells are shielded. Don't even think of opening it: the samples are, shall we say, temperamental.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_sakharov_2">
		<text>I'll manage.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_tools_0">
		<text>Kardan, did a stalker come by? From the group that settled in the bunker. For tools for a generator.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_tools_1">
		<text>Lom? He did... I gave him the tools, good ones, from the old days. Then we sat down and had a drink, as you do. And drunk as I was I ran my mouth: the test centre on Zaton I worked in, "Item 62"... He lit up. Said he'd go have a peek. Drunk, at nightfall.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_tools_2">
		<text>And then?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_tools_3">
		<text>Nothing. Not a word since. That centre is by the Iron Forest, the way down is by the crashed helicopter. He talked me out of my access card, but I kept a spare: here. If he went in there, it's bad. I'd like to know what became of him... I'm not one to go there anymore.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_tools_4">
		<text>I'll see what happened to him.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_pda_0">
		<text>I found Lom. In the test centre, dead. Here's his PDA.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_pda_1">
		<text>Ah... It was me who sent him there, with my tongue. Thanks for bringing it, at least now I know. Here, take this "Flash". It's no use to me, and you'll need it to start your generator.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="shelter_kardan_pda_2">
		<text>Thank you, Kardan.</text>
	</string>
