	<string id="st_shelter_brigadier_outfit_name">
		<text>The Brigadier's Nosorog</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_shelter_brigadier_outfit_descr">
		<text>The Nosorog exoskeleton of a mercenary everyone called the Brigadier. A professional who looked after his gear: the suit is upgraded to the limit, all five artefact containers are open and shielded, so no artefact radiation gets through and no applied modules are needed. Lightened to 18 kg.\n\nA module built into the helmet: a light (L), Oracle night vision (N), thermal vision (hold N) and an anomaly visor (J). It runs on the suit's accumulator: drag a battery onto the suit. With an electric artefact on the belt it runs on that, which also charges the accumulator and the PDA in its slot.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_shelter_brigadier_module_name">
		<text>Nosorog helmet module</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_shelter_brigadier_module_descr">
		<text>Built into the Brigadier's Nosorog helmet: a light, Oracle night vision, thermal vision and an anomaly visor. It can't be taken out; its charge is the suit's accumulator.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_shelter_brigadier_m4_name">
		<text>The Brigadier's M4 Tactical</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_shelter_brigadier_m4_descr">
		<text>The M4 Tactical carbine the Brigadier carried. Upgraded to the limit and well kept: it wears down from firing half as fast as an upgraded ordinary one, and the Chemist made it a quarter lighter. Any fitting scope goes onto its Picatinny rail; the Surefire silencer comes off.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="st_shelter_visor_on">
		<text>Anomaly visor on</text>
